content.description:
ROUND 1. Both sites re-verified as still lying on origin/main 142cbbf5a. Small, disjoint, clean.

THE EXEMPLAR ALREADY SHIPPED, WHICH IS WHY THESE TWO STAND OUT. #9599 (90b5ec4f5) repaired find-event so its receipt descends from the upstream write at all six exits. Its two siblings have no honesty commit at all.

(1) web/app/api/find/route.ts:27-29 - STILL LIES:
      27:  } catch {
      28:    // Empty suggestions is a harmless degrade - keep the existing default.
      29:    return NextResponse.json({ popular: [], nohits: [] });
    No descending field. THE EXEMPLAR IS IN THE SAME FILE at :56-60:
      56:  } catch (err) {
      57:    const message = err instanceof Error ? err.message : String(err);
      58:    return NextResponse.json(emptyResponse(engine, q, message), { status: 200 });
    ANCHOR CORRECTION: the original row said the exemplar is "ELEVEN LINES below". :56-60 is right; "eleven lines" is not - it is 27 lines from the catch at :27. Cite line numbers, never a distance; a distance is itself a receipt nobody can re-derive.

(2) web/app/api/search-seed/route.ts:46-49 - STILL LIES, and the judgment-call framing is intact:
      46:  } catch {
      49:    return { index: {}, docs: [] };
    Its declared consumer is still asserted verbatim at :18-20 ("an explicit fetchable endpoint for tooling / diagnostics"), and the HTTP GET at :25-27 returns the seed with no status distinction - so the declared consumer genuinely cannot tell engine-down from empty-corpus. The row's demand - REPAIR or CLASSIFY IN WRITING - is still live and still unanswered. If you classify, the writing must engage the declared tooling/diagnostics consumer, not wave at it.

POPULATION, re-derived: `git ls-tree -r --name-only origin/main web/app/api/` gives EXACTLY FIVE routes (admin/reindex, barkpark/webhook, find-event, find, search-seed) - the wave-48 correction to "three" holds today.

THE OTHER TWO ARE HONEST AND MUST NOT BE TOUCHED, confirmed this wave: barkpark/webhook/route.ts:164 returns `{ ok: true, revalidated: tags }` where tags is request-derived via tagsFor(payload) at :161 and revalidateTag returns void - lawful, nothing to descend from. admin/reindex has a real catch at :47 with a typed error body at :57.

FILES: web/app/api/find/route.ts, web/app/api/search-seed/route.ts (+ tests).
